Spec: Technical Debt Register

Purpose:
  Track unresolved correctness, coupling, agent-context, and migration risks in the current implementation without retaining completed work as active debt.

Owns:
  ./TECH-DEBT.md

References:
  ../speckit-specdd.sdd
  ./spec.sdd
  ./TODO.md

Must:
  The register contains unresolved risks only.
  Correctness risks distinguish deterministic authorization guarantees from agentic semantic concerns.
  The register identifies prose-derived authorization scope and dirty-state adoption as correctness risks until the native authorization model replaces them.
  The register identifies split authorization evidence as an atomicity risk.
  The register identifies duplicated SpecDD semantics and framework bootstrap context as migration debt rather than durable Boundary architecture.
  The register identifies current Spec Kit, SpecDD, and Codex naming leakage as adapter coupling.
  Entries state observable risk and preferred direction without duplicating detailed implementation plans from ./TODO.md.
  Completed risks are removed once current code, tests, and documentation establish the intended behavior.

Done when:
  Maintainers can identify the remaining correctness and migration hazards without reconstructing historical implementation TODO state.
